# Git: `autoagents` (stage) vs `prod` (production)

| Branch | Deploy target | URL |
|--------|---------------|-----|
| **`autoagents`** | Staging VPS (`/srv/serra/stage`) | https://stage-serra.ldeluipy.es |
| **`prod`** | Production VPS (`/srv/serra/prod`) | https://serra.ldeluipy.es |
| **`main`** | No auto-deploy — stable line; optional merge from `autoagents` | — |

Routine work: **`autoagents`**. Push → `stage.yml` runs tests; deploys staging when `STAGE_DEPLOY_ENABLED=true`.

Production: merge **`autoagents` → `prod`** only after cliente/dev sign-off on staging. Push **`prod`** → `prod.yml` (tests + Docker deploy when `DEPLOY_ENABLED=true`).

See **`docs/DEPLOY.md`** for SSH paths and GitHub secrets.

## Sync before you change anything

Run **`./scripts/git-sync-autoagents-branch.sh`** before the first edit and before **`git push`**.

## Where to commit

1. Checkout **`autoagents`** (or **`AGENT_GIT_BRANCH`**).
2. Commit and **`git push origin autoagents`**.
3. Do **not** push to **`prod`** for normal features.

## Promote to production

Merge to **`prod`** only when staging is validated (or explicit urgent/hotfix instruction). Prefer a PR **`autoagents` → `prod`**.

## Agents

- **Coder / tester:** Work on **`autoagents`**; verify on staging URL when possible.
- **Committer:** Push **`autoagents`**; merge **`prod`** only per release policy above.
- **User says “push”** without qualifier → push **`autoagents`**, not **`prod`**.
